# HISTORICAL REVIEW TEMPLATE: not used by the chosen two-VM implementation.
# The current network boundary is the separate Linux gateway's residential.nft.
# REVIEW TEMPLATE: standalone policy for a DEDICATED macOS guest only.
# Not loaded automatically. Do not replace a normal host's PF configuration with it.
# Do not call this an enforced kill switch until activation/state handling is verified.
# Static addressing/preconfigured routing assumed: no DHCP or shared-host forwarding.
# Existing PF states and rules must be reconciled before protected apps can start.

set block-policy drop
set skip on lo0

# Both IPv4 and IPv6, all interfaces, including newly appearing interfaces.
block drop all

# Only the encrypted TCP connection to the specified residential SS relay is allowed.
# TCP replies/related control traffic are handled by PF's connection state tracking.
pass out quick inet proto tcp from any to 198.51.100.24 port 26333 flags S/SA keep state
